<title>CHINA: China 1997 sugar shortage seen at 400,000 T.</title>
<headline>China 1997 sugar shortage seen at 400,000 T.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>China expects to have a 1997 sugar shortage of about 400,000 tonnes, the Futures Herald said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Some of the shortfall would be made up by imports, the newspaper said but gave no further details.</p>
<p>China imported 40,000 tonnes of sugar in January and February, down by 35.8 percent from the year-ago period, customs figures showed.</p>
<p>China imported 30,000 tonnes of sugar in February alone, the figures showed.</p>
<p>Output for the 1996/97 year was expected to reach 6.6 million tonnes, while consumption was estimated at 7.5 million tonnes with the shortfall to be made up mainly from reserves, an earlier report said.</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
